
Chief: So I was saying... One evening he was trusted with a delivery for the generals suprise birthday party. His directions were simple, to deliver a special cargo of the officer's wives, an all-female orchestral quintet and a crate of fine malt whiskey for the upcoming celebration.

Mayor: Sounds like quite a party.

Chief: Yes. Except something went wrong. The weather was fine, the plane in top shape but an unknown failure - still being investigated - caused Harlow to ditch into the sea near a deserted island. The plane was lost but the passengers managed to make it to shore.

Mayor: Good god! Was anyone hurt?

Chief: The facts aren't completely clear. When the rescue party arrived the women were found to be suffering from dehydration and exhaustion.

Mayor: Still, they were lucky to survive so far from civilisation. I don't see how Harlow can be blamed.

Chief: The rescue party only took 14 hours to arrive! Harlow was found passed out in shrubbery wearing only his underpants... the trombonist was unable to perform for a month!

Mayor: ......

Chief: When he woke up he had lost his pilots licence and found himself heading the Federal Monkey Patrol. He's a loose cannon with enemies in high places and when this is over I want to make sure he goes back to that basement and never flies again.


picture giant_claw2.jpg

Mayor: Well done Harlow, good work! But it's not over yet, there are still dozens of other apes elsewhere in the city.

Harlow: There's nothing a few wings, a propeller & a machine gun can't fix. 

Boffin: Sweet pen protector, look at the radar

Chief: Good god, what do you suppose that giant thing was?

Boffin: The radar shows a massive object shaped like a bird approaching. From our readings it appears to have a wingspan of over 200 metres!

Harlow: Meters? Enough of your scientific mumbo jumbo, this is America, give me measurements I can understand!

Boffin: From wingtip to wingtip it is over 600 feet across

Harlow: I said units I can understand! <shakes fist>

Boffin: .....as big as a battleship.

Harlow: (whistles in awe) Well that settles it, it's obviously an antimatter extraterrestrial buzzard from another galaxy. It must have come here in search for a place to nest & nurture it's young. I call it The Giant Claw & it too must be exterminated.......... by me & my trusty plane.

Chief: Good god! There's no way you can bring that down with your plane! Harlow, you MUST relinquish control & let the army handle this. You can't do this alone!

Harlow: I think you underestimate this old skybird.

Boffin: I doubt you can even scratch that thing, I would keep out of it's way if I were you. If you see or hear the beast the best thing to do is fly as low as you can between the skyscrapers to shake it off.

Mayor: Ok you heard the man Harlow, thin out the monkeys but watch out for the giant claw!

Harlow: I can smell their bullet riddled rotting caresses now. To freedom!

